<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.4.1: Using Function Notation in Tables of Values</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00899</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.4.1: Using Function Notation in Tables of Values</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a55e751d-2a9b-480d-8f4b-ad3a42f47764</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>Use the tables to answer each question.</para>
<table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
       \(x\)
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
       \(f(x)=10-2x\)
      </entry>
	  </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
       1
      </entry>
      <entry>
     8
		  
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
       1.5
      </entry>
      <entry>
        7
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
       5
      </entry>
      <entry>
       0
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
       –2
      </entry>
      <entry>
      14
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
<table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
     \(x\)
      </entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">
     \(g(x)=x^3\)
      </entry>
	  </row></thead><tbody>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>–2</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>–8</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>0</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>0</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>1</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>1</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        <para>3</para>
      </entry>
      <entry>
        <para>27</para>
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What do you notice? </para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
    <list>
      <item>
        The tables don't say “input” and “output.”</item>
      <item>
        While there is a column labeled \(x\), there is not a column labeled \(y\).</item>
      <item>
        One function is called \(f\). The other is called \(g\).</item>
      <item>
        There’s an expression (rather than a number) on the right side of the equation \(f(x)=10−2x\) and \(g(x)=x^3\).
      </item>
      <item>
        If we substitute the values in the left column for the \(x\) in the expression, we get the values in the right column.
      </item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What do you wonder?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
    <list>
      <item>
        Why is \(x\) on the right side of the equal sign?
      </item>
      <item>
        Are there rules about how to name functions?
      </item>
      <item>
        What does each equation, \(f(x)=10-2x\) and \(g(x)=x^3\), mean?
      </item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
